cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Counterfactual Evidence Audits Predict LLM-Agent Susceptibility to Ranked Context"
message: "If you use this work, please cite the paper below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Usman"
    given-names: "Rana Muhammad"
    email: "usmanashrafrana@gmail.com"
abstract: >
  We introduce a five-document counterfactual evidence audit that predicts
  responses to disjoint 45-document contexts in held-out open-weight
  model-task cells. Matched controls isolate evidence composition from order,
  cross-interface tests evaluate transfer to static RAG, and a separate Codex
  study identifies a deployed-agent boundary. The validated claim is a
  domain-specific triage procedure for one synthetic remote-work corpus.
keywords:
  - large language models
  - LLM agents
  - retrieval-augmented generation
  - recommender systems
  - evidence selection
  - behavioral auditing
  - agent security
